# netsurf: inline <svg> painted with libsvgtiny (vb_inline_svg.c)
#
# MacSurf built boxes for inline <svg> (SVG_INLINE) but painted them only on
# Mac OS 9, so every inline icon and logo -- Google's logo, YouTube's icons,
# most sites' buttons -- was blank. The element's DOM subtree is serialised
# back to SVG markup and parsed by libsvgtiny at the box's size; shapes are
# plotted as the SVG image handler does. currentColor becomes the CSS colour,
# a root with no fill fills with it (icon sets use "fill: currentColor" in
# CSS), and <use href="#id"> targets are copied into a <defs>. Parsed
# diagrams are cached by box, node, size and reconvert sequence.
